WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.692
Idea. Take six plus nine. You can take out the common factor three, and write three times, two plus three. Taking out a factor means writing something as a factor times a bracket.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:26.859
The binomial series expands a bracket to a negative or fractional power. It only works if the bracket starts with one. So take the first number out. Two plus three x becomes two times, one plus three over two x.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:41.285
The key rule: the factor you take out gets the same power as the bracket. A negative power means a reciprocal, and a fractional power means a root. Two to the minus one is a half. Eight to the one third is two.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:48.887
The question says express in the form p times, one plus q x, to the power n. Find p and q.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:59.015
Method. Step one: write any root or fraction as a single power. Step two: take the first number out, and divide the x term by it.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:06.765
Step three: give the power to both factors, and work out c to the power n. Step four: read off p and q.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:13.367
The traps: forgetting to give the outside factor the power, and forgetting to divide the x term.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:27.808
Worked example. June twenty twenty two. Two plus three x, to the power minus one, is expressed as p times, one plus q x, to the power minus one. Find p and q. Two marks.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:34.459
Step one: take out the two. Two plus three x is two times, one plus three over two x.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:42.695
Step two: give the power to both factors. Two to the minus one, times one plus three over two x, to the minus one.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:49.378
Step three: two to the minus one is one half. So p is one half, and q is three over two.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:59.099
Check with x equals nought. The left side is two to the minus one, which is a half. The right side is a half times one, which is also a half.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:07.311
A tempting wrong route leaves the two without the power. At x equals nought that gives two, not a half. So it is wrong.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:16.060
So p is one half and q is three over two. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:30.343
Common mistake. A common mistake is to take two out but not divide the x term. At x equals one, the left side is a fifth, but the wrong form gives one eighth. Divide three x by two.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:50.026
Your turn. Now you try, from January twenty twenty three. Eight plus three x, to the power one third, is written as p times, one plus q x, to the power one third. Find p and q. A power of a third means a cube root. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:03:00.063
Answer. Take eight out. Eight plus three x is eight times, one plus three over eight x. Give the power one third to both factors.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:12.809
Eight to the one third is the cube root of eight, which is two. So p is two and q is three over eight. Check with x equals nought: the cube root of eight is two, and two times one is two.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:21.018
The common wrong answer is p equals eight, forgetting the power. At x equals nought, the left side is two, not eight.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:28.991
Remember: take the first number out, divide the x term by it, give both factors the power, and read off p and q.
